      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Set your player size in the rift settings and VRC to what you would have when not in a wheelchair. Then you can use the standing/seated toggle in the quick menu to crouch. Thats what I do when I'm not standing in VRChat.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-10-18T09:55:35.915Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I'm disabled, so stuck in a wheelchair. VRChat with Rift lets me somewhat forget that. However, since I am playing from a wheelchair, I cannot crouch down to the floor.\nOn desktop, this doesn't matter because I can use a key to toggle prone or crouch. But in Rift+Touch, there is no option for me.\n\nSo wondering whether there could be a control option in the settings menu in-game to allow for one control (maybe pressing a thumbstick, or de-mirror a button on one side) to allow cycling between standing, crouching and prone?\n\nAlso, every time I go to a new world I have to manually switch it to seated play again, no matter if I was already in seated play in the previous world. Is there a way to make this setting global, so if I set seated play when I open VRChat it will stay like that until I close it or select Standing manually again?\n\nThanks.",
